<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-13">13 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Avezzano earthquake devastates central Italy</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 6.7 earthquake struck the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzo</a> region, killing about 30,000 people. In Avezzano itself almost all of the population perished.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-18">18 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan presents its Twenty-One Demands to China</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> secretly pressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a>'s government for extensive rights in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and beyond. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> accepted a reduced version under ultimatum, fuelling Chinese nationalism against Japan.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-19">19 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Zeppelins bomb Britain for the first time</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/airship">airships</a> dropped bombs on Great Yarmouth, Sheringham and King's Lynn in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norfolk">Norfolk</a>, killing four civilians. It was the first air raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, opening a new front in the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-24">24 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British battlecruisers defeat a German squadron at Dogger Bank</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Forewarned by codebreakers, Admiral Beatty's battlecruisers intercepted a German raiding force in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> and sank the armoured cruiser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher">Blücher</a>. Signalling errors let the rest escape.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-8">8 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">'The Birth of a Nation' premieres in Los Angeles</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">D. W. Griffith's Civil War epic pioneered techniques of film storytelling but glorified the Ku Klux Klan. It drew protests from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naacp">NAACP</a> and helped inspire the Klan's revival that year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-19">19 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Allied fleet begins bombarding the Dardanelles forts</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French warships opened fire on Ottoman forts guarding the straits, hoping to force a way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. The naval effort failed in March, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli</a> landings.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-22">22 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany releases chlorine gas at Ypres</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German troops released chlorine from cylinders against French and Algerian positions near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ypres">Ypres</a>. It was the first large-scale use of lethal gas on the Western Front and opened a chemical arms race.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-24">24 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ottoman authorities arrest Armenian leaders in Constantinople</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hundreds of Armenian intellectuals and community leaders were rounded up and deported, most later killed. The date marks the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenian-genocide">Armenian genocide</a>, in which around a million people died.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-25">25 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Allied troops land at Gallipoli</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British, French, Australian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> troops landed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli peninsula</a>. The campaign failed after eight months and around 100,000 deaths on both sides; 25 April is now Anzac Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-26">26 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Italy signs the secret Treaty of London with the Entente</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> concluded a secret agreement with the United Kingdom, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, promising to enter the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> on the Entente side within a month in return for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trentino">Trentino</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-tyrol">South Tyrol</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a>, Istria, part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and other gains.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-london-1915">Treaty of London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-7">7 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">German U-boat sinks the liner Lusitania</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">U-20 torpedoed the Cunard liner off southern Ireland, sinking her in 18 minutes with the loss of 1,198 lives, 128 of them American. Outrage in the US turned opinion sharply against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-12">12 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germans execute the British nurse Edith Cavell</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A German firing squad in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> executed Edith Cavell, who had helped some 200 Allied soldiers escape occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. Her death caused international outrage and became a powerful theme of Allied propaganda.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-celaya" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-celaya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-celaya">Battle of Celaya</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Celaya, in April 1915, was a pair of engagements near Celaya in Guanajuato in which Constitutionalist forces under Álvaro Obregón defeated Pancho Villa's Division of the North.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-darin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-darin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-darin">Treaty of Darin</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Darin was signed on 26 December 1915 on the island of Tarut between Britain, represented by Percy Cox, and Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kyakhta-1915" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kyakhta-1915.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kyakhta-1915">Treaty of Kyakhta (1915)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Kyakhta of 1915 was a tripartite agreement between Russia, the Republic of China and Mongolia, signed at the border town of Kyakhta in June 1915.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/carpenter-agreement">Carpenter Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Carpenter Agreement was signed on 22 March 1915 between Frank W. Carpenter, American governor of the Department of Mindanao and Sulu, and Sultan Jamalul Kiram II of Sulu.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mongua">Battle of Mongua</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Mongua was fought on 18–20 August 1915 in southern Angola between a Portuguese army under General António Pereira de Eça and the forces of the Kwanyama king Mandume ya Ndemufayo.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sam-khubis">Battle of Sam Khubis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Sam Khubis was fought on 8 May 1915 in central Namibia between the Rehoboth Basters and German colonial troops.</p></div></li></ol></section>
