<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Commonwealth%20of%20Australia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Commonwealth of Australia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Australian and New Zealand troops land at Gallipoli on 25 April</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Italy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Italy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Italy enters the First World War on the side of the Entente</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sulu-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sulu%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sulu Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jamalul Kiram II gives up temporal power under the Carpenter Agreement</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/union-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Union%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Union of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">South African forces conquer German South West Africa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-haiti"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Haiti.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Haiti</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After President Vilbrun Guillaume Sam's execution of 167 prisoners and his lynching, US Marines land at Port-au-Prince; the occupation lasts until 1934.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/yazidism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Yazidism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Yazidism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">During the Armenian genocide many Yazidis are killed, and others flee from Van, Kars and Bazîd to Transcaucasia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/haitian-vodou"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Haitian%20Vodou.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Haitian Vodou</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United States occupies Haiti until 1934, stirring foreign interest in Vodou and its reassessment by Haitian indigenists</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/may-fourth-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/May%20Fourth%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>May Fourth Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan’s Twenty-One Demands become known to the Chinese public and provoke anti-Japanese feeling</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/fascism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fascism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fascism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The term “fascism” is first used by members of Mussolini’s Fasces of Revolutionary Action</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-arabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Arabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Arabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Hussein–McMahon Correspondence begins: Britain will support Arab independence if the Mashreq Arabs revolt against the Ottomans</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/mahatma-gandhi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mahatma%20Gandhi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mahatma Gandhi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He returns to India at the request of Gopal Krishna Gokhale and joins the Indian National Congress</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/congress-poland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Congress%20Poland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Congress Poland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Russian army retreats and the Central Powers occupy the kingdom</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-serbia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Serbia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Serbia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Austro-Hungarian, German and Bulgarian troops occupy Serbia; the army retreats through Albania to Corfu</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/stonehenge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Stonehenge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Stonehenge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cecil Chubb bought the site at auction and gave it to the nation three years later</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/portuguese-angola"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Portuguese%20Angola.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Portuguese Angola</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">General António Júlio da Costa Pereira de Eça's campaign reoccupies southern Angola after the German-backed Ovambo Uprising</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/winston-churchill"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Winston%20Churchill.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Winston Churchill</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The naval attack on the Dardanelles and the Gallipoli campaign fail, and he is removed from the Admiralty</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Resources are taken from the forts of Verdun, and the railway line from Paris is closed by the German 3rd Army in mid-July</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/gyeongju"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gyeongju.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gyeongju</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A museum, the forerunner of the Gyeongju National Museum, opens to show the finds from the excavated tombs</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/edicts-of-ashoka"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Edicts%20of%20Ashoka.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Edicts of Ashoka</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">An inscription found at Maski confirms that the title Devanampiya belongs to Ashoka</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/albert-einstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Albert%20Einstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Albert Einstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Proposes the general theory of relativity, extending his mechanics to include gravitation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/new-culture-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Culture%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Culture Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Chen Duxiu founds the Youth Magazine, later retitled New Youth, marking the beginning of the movement</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-somme"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Somme.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Somme</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Chantilly Conference agrees simultaneous Allied offensives for 1916 and the Franco-British contribution is planned for the Somme</span></li></ul></section>
